# Optional. Only needed if you are NOT using OAuth.
#
# Preferred: log in once with
#     python -m kaggle auth login
# which caches credentials in ~/.kaggle/credentials.json and refreshes them
# automatically. Nothing needs to go in this file in that case.
#
# Fallback: generate a token at https://www.kaggle.com/settings/api
# ("Generate New Token" under "API") and paste the token string below.
#
# Note: kaggle CLI 2.2+ uses a single API token. The older
# KAGGLE_USERNAME / KAGGLE_KEY pair is no longer supported.
#
# Either way you must accept the competition rules at
# kaggle.com/competitions/nfl-big-data-bowl-2027 or downloads return 403.
KAGGLE_API_TOKEN=
